<title>THAILAND: Asia Securities asks for share trading resumption.</title>
<headline>Asia Securities asks for share trading resumption.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thai broker Asia Securities Trading on Thursday asked the Stock Exchange of Thailand to permit trading in the company's shares to resume.</p>
<p>ABN-AMRO Hoare Govett Asia (Holdings) Ltd on Wednesday made a 35 baht per share tender offer for up to 49 percent of AST's stock. At the company's request the shares were suspended on Wednesday morning at 24 baht.</p>
<p>&quot;The information has been disseminated among the general public...We hereby request a revocation of the trading suspension of the shares of Asia Securities Trading Plc,&quot; the firm said in a statement.</p>
<p>($1 = 26 baht)</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
